  "presentation_summary": [
    "29-year-old woman with schizoaffective disorder, bipolar disorder, and multiple prior suicide attempts presented after intentional ingestion of 300 acetylsalicylic acid 325 mg tablets 3 to 4 hours before ED arrival.",
    "She developed generalized abdominal pain, nonbilious nonbloody vomiting, dry heaving, confusion, tachypnea, and marked tachycardia; she denied vertigo and tinnitus.",
    "Admission evaluation showed mixed respiratory alkalosis and metabolic acidosis with pH 7.542, pCO2 24.5 mmHg, bicarbonate 15 mmol/L, anion gap 16, urine pH 7.6, and salicylate 98.2 mg/dL.",
    "Because of severe salicylate level and altered mental status, she received bicarbonate infusion and slow low-efficiency hemodialysis; activated charcoal was withheld due to vomiting and aspiration risk.",
    "After initial dialysis the salicylate level rebounded to 129.7 mg/dL with worsening confusion, requiring regular hemodialysis followed by SLED."
  ],
